# Liberated Bread DNS blocklist: profile 'updates', all devices, format 'routeros'
# Generated from cloud.egress in https://github.com/liberatedbread/liberatedbread-protocol-specs
# by scripts/generate_blocklists.py. Do not edit this file; fix the spec.
#
# Firmware update hosts only, so the rest of the vendor cloud, and the vendor app away
# from home, usually keeps working; where a device's update offer rides its main cloud
# link, that link is listed too. It stops the update hosts the specs NAME; vendors move
# update traffic without notice, so this is the weakest list here.
#
# A DNS list is the second layer. A device that ignores your resolver walks
# straight past it, so firewall the device as well: https://liberatedbread.com/firewall/
#
# RouterOS 7.5 or later (match-subdomain). Import with /import. Every entry is tagged
# 'liberatedbread:all:' and the first command removes that tag's previous import, so
# re-running this list replaces it, and lists for different devices coexist. A time
# redirect answers A only; AAAA still comes from upstream.
#
# Devices:
#   June Intelligent Oven (june-oven)
#   LG webOS TV Second Screen Protocol (lg-webos)
#   TP-Link Kasa Smart Plug (tplink-kasa-smart-plug)
#
# Time sources. NOT blocked: a device that loses its clock loses its schedules.
# Point these at a LAN NTP server (your router, or chrony on any always-on host),
# or regenerate with --time-server <address> to have the redirect written for you:
#   pool.ntp.org (and subdomains)  [tplink-kasa-smart-plug | time | reported]
#   time.nist.gov  [tplink-kasa-smart-plug | time | reported]
#
# Left out, because blocking them breaks the device or its clock:
#   - lgtvsdp.com (lg-webos): The TV takes its clock from this service — a header on its
#     HTTPS API rather than NTP — and the Content Store, app updates and home-screen
#     configuration live here too. Blocked, the clock resets after a cold boot (to
#     2019-12-31 on one report) and apps then fail their certificate checks.
#   - nextlgsdp.com (lg-webos): The newer SDP family: blocking it is reported to stop
#     the TV setting its clock and to disable the Content Store.
#
# Each rule below is preceded by: devices | roles | verification.
# 'reported' and 'hypothesis' entries have not been observed by this project.

/ip dns static
remove [find where comment~"^liberatedbread:all:"]
add name=dev-devices-ota.junelife.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: june-oven"
add name=devices-ota.walker-cloud.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: june-oven"
add name=download.tplinkcloud.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: tplink-kasa-smart-plug"
add name=messaging.junelife.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: june-oven"
add name=nsu.lge.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: lg-webos"
add name=snu.lge.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: lg-webos"
add name=su-dev.lge.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: lg-webos"
add name=su-ssl.lge.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: lg-webos"
add name=su.lge.com type=NXDOMAIN comment="liberatedbread:all: lg-webos"
